Optimized kernels
-----------------
The files under opendde/model/optimized/ are adapted from the OpenDDE
optimization kit, Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.

Portions of opendde/model/optimized/trimul.py restate the arithmetic of the
pair-stack modules of Protenix (https://github.com/bytedance/Protenix),
Copyright 2024 ByteDance and/or its affiliates, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. No Protenix source file is included.

opendde/model/optimized/triattn_exact.py and csrc/triattn_v3.cu reproduce the
results of cuEquivariance's triangle_attention; they were written against its
observable numerics and contain no cuEquivariance source.

opendde/model/optimized/triattn_native.py and csrc/triattn_sm80/ are the
kit's triattn_native (v11) sm_80 member, trimmed to head dimension 32.

opendde/model/optimized/transition.py follows the arithmetic of OpenDDE's
own Transition module, itself derived from Protenix (Apache License 2.0).

opendde/model/optimized/dit_fused.py follows the arithmetic of OpenDDE's own
DiffusionTransformer, itself derived from Protenix (Apache License 2.0); its
Triton row kernels are adapted from the kit's fused token-stack kernels.

These kernels call, and do not include, NVIDIA cuEquivariance (NVIDIA's
licence, as installed), PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause) and Triton (MIT).
